      "marks_note": "a person pressing a key when something looked wrong. Every mark is placed against the nearest preceding stall, because the first flown trace came back with every one of its marks inside two seconds of a rebuild: the flyer was marking a freeze, not the far field. `marks_after_a_stall` equal to `marks` means this flight measured the harness and says nothing about what is visible; well under it means the marks are about the view.",
